WEBVTT

00:00:00.614 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.635 --> 00:00:05.710
Today, we start the skin care course with something many people rush through:

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:08.110
skin analysis and consultation.

00:00:08.503 --> 00:00:10.190
Every good treatment starts here.

00:00:10.458 --> 00:00:14.590
Read the skin correctly, and you choose the right products, and the right method.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.212
Read it wrong, and however expensive the products are,

00:00:18.162 --> 00:00:20.510
the client's skin can still end up red,

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.790
stinging and breaking out, and the client won't come back.

00:00:24.411 --> 00:00:26.526
Here is something that happens all the time:

00:00:26.874 --> 00:00:30.686
a client walks in and says, my skin is really oily.

00:00:31.038 --> 00:00:34.824
The therapist hears that, and goes straight for a strong cleanser,

00:00:34.774 --> 00:00:36.126
a thorough exfoliation,

00:00:36.316 --> 00:00:38.446
and then an oil-absorbing clay mask.

00:00:38.795 --> 00:00:40.926
The next day, the client messages:

00:00:41.196 --> 00:00:45.966
my skin feels tight and stinging, it is flaking, and it is still shiny.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.246
So what went wrong?

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:49.246
That skin is not only oily;

00:00:49.565 --> 00:00:51.006
it is also dehydrated.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:55.406
Strip away all the oil, and the skin gets even drier and tighter.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:01:00.206
The therapist only listened, without looking, touching, or asking more.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.546
So the first thing to understand:

00:01:02.757 --> 00:01:05.986
skin type and skin condition are two different things.

00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:08.306
Skin type is the skin's nature:

00:01:08.497 --> 00:01:11.106
fairly stable, and mostly down to genetics:

00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:15.346
normal, dry, oily, combination, and sensitive.

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:18.546
Skin condition, on the other hand, changes:

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.638
with the season, the weather, the products the client is using, with age,

00:01:23.588 --> 00:01:24.626
and with sleep.

00:01:25.055 --> 00:01:27.666
Dehydrated today, it may be fine next month.

00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:29.182
Normal skin:

00:01:29.364 --> 00:01:33.342
smooth, small pores, not too shiny, not tight.

00:01:34.024 --> 00:01:34.942
Dry skin:

00:01:35.288 --> 00:01:39.453
little oil, feels slightly rough, easily feels tight after cleansing,

00:01:39.403 --> 00:01:41.182
sometimes with light flaking.

00:01:41.747 --> 00:01:42.622
Oily skin:

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.542
shiny all over, larger pores, prone to blackheads.

00:01:47.129 --> 00:01:48.222
Combination skin:

00:01:48.595 --> 00:01:52.113
shiny in the T zone, meaning the forehead, nose and chin,

00:01:52.063 --> 00:01:54.302
while the cheeks are normal, or dry.

00:01:54.849 --> 00:01:55.822
Sensitive skin:

00:01:56.158 --> 00:02:00.538
reddens easily, stings easily, and itches easily when changing products,

00:02:00.488 --> 00:02:02.222
or when the weather changes.

00:02:02.815 --> 00:02:05.668
As for skin conditions, a few are the most common.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.028
Dehydration:

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:12.468
the skin feels tight, looks dull, has very fine lines, and can still be oily.

00:02:12.852 --> 00:02:13.428
Remember:

00:02:13.538 --> 00:02:17.668
lacking oil means dry skin, but any skin type can be dehydrated.

00:02:18.241 --> 00:02:20.948
Redness, with small visible blood vessels.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:21.988
Congestion:

00:02:22.257 --> 00:02:24.628
blackheads, and tiny bumps under the skin.

00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:25.908
Pigmentation:

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:28.788
brown spots, freckles, dark marks.

00:02:29.134 --> 00:02:30.148
And signs of aging:

00:02:30.329 --> 00:02:32.788
wrinkles, and skin that is less firm.

00:02:33.397 --> 00:02:34.876
So how do you read the skin?

00:02:35.199 --> 00:02:38.396
With your eyes, your hands, and your questions.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:43.173
Analyze the skin when it is clean, with no makeup, in good light,

00:02:43.123 --> 00:02:44.636
with a magnifying lamp.

00:02:45.225 --> 00:02:48.796
Cover the eyes with cotton pads, because the lamp is very bright.

00:02:49.452 --> 00:02:53.832
Look at whether the surface is smooth or rough, where the pores are larger,

00:02:53.782 --> 00:02:55.276
and which areas are oily.

00:02:55.827 --> 00:02:57.436
Then touch very lightly:

00:02:57.926 --> 00:03:00.796
is the skin soft, tight, or rough?

00:03:01.044 --> 00:03:04.716
Any spot that turns pink as soon as you touch it is sensitive right now.

00:03:05.344 --> 00:03:06.643
Looking is not enough.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.083
The consultation form is what helps you avoid the biggest risks.

00:03:10.413 --> 00:03:11.363
Ask the client:

00:03:11.604 --> 00:03:14.803
any allergies, any past reactions to cosmetics?

00:03:15.121 --> 00:03:16.563
What medication are they taking?

00:03:16.937 --> 00:03:20.704
What are they using on their skin at home, especially retinoids,

00:03:20.654 --> 00:03:21.923
or exfoliating acids?

00:03:22.263 --> 00:03:24.643
Are they taking the acne medicine isotretinoin?

00:03:24.978 --> 00:03:29.603
Have they had any recent treatments, like a chemical peel, laser, or waxing?

00:03:29.777 --> 00:03:31.523
And do they spend a lot of time in the sun?

00:03:32.152 --> 00:03:33.851
Why ask in so much detail?

00:03:34.089 --> 00:03:38.411
Skin on retinoids or acids is thinner and more sensitive than usual.

00:03:38.674 --> 00:03:42.331
Exfoliate it hard, and it easily gets scratched and sore.

00:03:42.733 --> 00:03:47.051
If the client is taking isotretinoin, the skin is very easily damaged.

00:03:47.474 --> 00:03:50.251
The lesson on when not to treat a client made it clear:

00:03:50.439 --> 00:03:54.571
no waxing while taking the medicine, and for about six months afterwards.

00:03:54.752 --> 00:03:58.175
And if the client is pregnant, that is a reason to ask more,

00:03:58.125 --> 00:04:01.211
and to choose products exactly as the brand instructs.

00:04:01.383 --> 00:04:04.331
No guessing, and no drawing your own conclusions.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.268
And here is the most important principle for anyone who works with skin:

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:10.428
we do not diagnose.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:17.589
If you see sunburn, broken skin, a cold sore on the lip, an area that is swollen,

00:04:17.539 --> 00:04:18.668
red, painful,

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:23.234
or has pus, or an unusual mole that is changing color or shape,

00:04:23.184 --> 00:04:24.908
don't work on that area.

00:04:25.258 --> 00:04:26.748
Do not name a disease.

00:04:27.097 --> 00:04:30.428
Describe what you see, and suggest the client ask a doctor.

00:04:30.614 --> 00:04:33.788
The lesson on when not to treat a client covers this in detail.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.194
Only after reading the skin and listening to the client do you choose the treatment.

00:04:38.664 --> 00:04:40.274
And be honest about results.

00:04:40.702 --> 00:04:44.354
A facial leaves the skin clean, soft, and fresher.

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.483
But brown spots, wrinkles,

00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:50.354
or long-standing acne don't disappear after a single session.

00:04:50.786 --> 00:04:53.474
Promise too much, and the client will be disappointed.

00:04:53.737 --> 00:04:55.874
Be honest, and the client will trust you.

00:04:56.112 --> 00:04:59.074
Write down the client's goals, so you can compare next time.

00:04:59.702 --> 00:05:04.365
Results in the salon only last if the client looks after her skin properly at home.

00:05:04.946 --> 00:05:06.445
Give the client a simple plan:

00:05:06.707 --> 00:05:10.215
a gentle cleanser, a moisturizer that suits her skin type,

00:05:10.165 --> 00:05:11.885
and sunscreen every morning.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.445
Just a few steps, but done consistently.

00:05:14.803 --> 00:05:16.685
Don't sell the client ten products.

00:05:17.051 --> 00:05:20.605
Then book the next visit, so you can see together how the skin has changed.

00:05:21.202 --> 00:05:23.097
Finally, the client record.

00:05:23.628 --> 00:05:28.137
What the client tells you about allergies, medication and health is private.

00:05:28.554 --> 00:05:32.697
Only write it down if the client agrees, and keep it strictly confidential.

00:05:33.205 --> 00:05:37.379
You can keep this in VaraaAi, in the internal notes on the client record,

00:05:37.329 --> 00:05:39.017
which only the salon can see.

00:05:39.436 --> 00:05:42.457
Next time, whoever treats the client will know right away:

00:05:42.638 --> 00:05:46.537
what the skin is like, what has been used, and how it reacted.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:50.935
So you see, skin analysis is not a quick glance for the sake of it.

00:05:51.181 --> 00:05:55.655
It is looking, touching, and asking, and only then deciding.

00:05:56.244 --> 00:06:00.913
In the practice lesson, we will do a skin analysis and consultation for a client,

00:06:00.863 --> 00:06:01.655
step by step.

00:06:02.164 --> 00:06:05.015
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:05.347 --> 00:06:06.215
See you next time.
